---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import WhatsAppCTA from '../components/WhatsAppCTA.astro';
import { SITE } from '../config/site';
import { generalLink } from '../lib/whatsapp';
---

<Base title="About" description={`About ${SITE.brand}. ${SITE.tagline}.`}>
  <section class="section">
    <div class="shell measure">
      <span class="eyebrow">About</span>
      <h1 style="margin-top:0.5rem;">Chosen with care, sold in conversation.</h1>

      <p class="lede" style="margin-top:1.2rem;">
        {SITE.brand} selects jewelry and accessories from makers we rate, and buys in quantities
        small enough that we know every piece we carry.
      </p>

      <h3 style="margin-top:2.4rem; margin-bottom:0.7rem;">Why there’s no checkout</h3>
      <p style="margin-bottom:1rem;">
        Most of what we sell needs one question answered before it ships: a ring size, a chain
        length, which stone, whether it’s being engraved. Shopping carts are bad at questions.
        WhatsApp is good at them.
      </p>
      <p style="margin-bottom:1rem;">
        So every piece on this site has an enquiry button instead of an add-to-cart. It opens a chat
        with the piece already named, and we take it from there.
      </p>

      <h3 style="margin-top:2.4rem; margin-bottom:0.7rem;">Ordered in</h3>
      <p style="margin-bottom:1rem;">
        Pieces marked <em>ordered in</em> aren’t held in stock. We place the order once you’ve
        decided. That usually means two to four weeks, and it means you get a say in the details
        along the way: for stone-set pieces we send photographs of what’s available so you pick the
        one you want.
      </p>

      <h3 style="margin-top:2.4rem; margin-bottom:0.7rem;">Care</h3>
      <p style="margin-bottom:1.6rem;">
        Keep pieces dry, store them apart so chains don’t knot, and take gold vermeil off before
        swimming. If something we sold you goes wrong, tell us and we’ll help you sort it.
      </p>

      <WhatsAppCTA href={generalLink()} label="Ask us anything" />
    </div>
  </section>
</Base>
